<title>UK: NatWest still to decide on UK rate move.</title>
<headline>NatWest still to decide on UK rate move.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's National Westminster Bank Plc said on Friday it had not decided if it would alter its rates in response to the Bank of England's decision to raise official interest rates to 6.5 percent from 6.25 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;We are still looking into it,&quot; a NatWest spokeswoman told Reuters.  </p>
<p>NatWest's banking rival Barclays Plc said it had raised base interest rates by 25 basis points to 6.5 percent with immediate effect.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
